  "details": "Desktop mouse movements when in game are behaving very strangely (Desktop mode only obviously). The speed of the mouse is greatly slowed compared to the mouse speed outside application requiring you to lift the mouse several times to do a full revolution in game. The mouse sensitivity slider is already at 100% and I shouldn't have to change all my OS settings defaults and mess up my work flow on all other applications because VRC is doing weird stuff. I think the sensitivity is just too low by default. The really weird thing which makes me think its a bug is when you open the menu, the speed returns to what you would expect. Its only in game that the speed greatly slows. Also, I tried a second mouse and this one despite working perfectly everywhere else makes jarring jumps in game when rotating. I do believe something is up with mouse movement in the latest version.",
